{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1525809985,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMjEzMjg0MzU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2482","origin":"github"},"title":"Result filter is not recognized","message":"I want to set up a result filter, but I'm not having any luck in getting it executed.\n\nSay I have the following extension:\n\n```python\nfrom datalad.interface.base import Interface\nfrom datalad.interface.base import build_doc\nfrom datalad.interface.results import get_status_dict\n\n\n@build_doc\nclass Foo(Interface):\n    from datalad.distribution.dataset import EnsureDataset\n    from datalad.interface.utils import eval_results\n    from datalad.support.constraints import EnsureNone\n    from datalad.support.param import Parameter\n\n    result_filter = lambda x: \"blah\" in x\n\n    _params_ = dict(\n        dataset=Parameter(\n            args=(\"-d\", \"--dataset\"),\n            doc=\"\"\"\"dataset to foo.\"\"\",\n            constraints=EnsureDataset() | EnsureNone()),\n    )\n\n    @staticmethod\n    @eval_results\n    def __call__(dataset=None):\n        yield get_status_dict(\"foo\",\n                              message=\"has blah\",\n                              type=\"dataset\",\n                              path=dataset.path if dataset else \"nowhere\",\n                              status=\"ok\",\n                              blah=\"aaaa\")\n        yield get_status_dict(\"foo\",\n                              message=\"no blah\",\n                              type=\"dataset\",\n                              path=dataset.path if dataset else \"nowhere\",\n                              status=\"ok\")\n\n\n__datalad_plugin__ = Foo\n```\n\nThe key bit is the `result_filter` assignment above. With that filter, I want to limit the results to records that have the key \"blah\". But it isn't being executed.\n\n```\n% datalad -ldebug foo\n[DEBUG  ] Determined class of decorated function: \u003cclass 'datalad.plugin.foo.Foo'\u003e\nfoo(ok): nowhere (dataset) [has blah]\nfoo(ok): nowhere (dataset) [no blah]\naction summary:\n  foo (ok: 2)\n```\n\nThe `result_filter` argument passed to `_process_results` is `None`. It seems like this issue is here:\n\n\u003chttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/43e37edc6f00b6edf250f1edc0116b9bd62f3f87/datalad/interface/utils.py#L333-L337\u003e\n\nMy filter is in `_func_class.result_filter`, but it doesn't get reached because `kwargs` has a `result_filter` key with a value of `None`, so the `pop` returns `None`.\n\nAlthough I doubt it's the right thing to do generally, if I let things fall back to `_func_class.result_filter` with\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/datalad/interface/utils.py b/datalad/interface/utils.py\nindex f9e305b47..46d0ef903 100644\n--- a/datalad/interface/utils.py\n+++ b/datalad/interface/utils.py\n@@ -331,9 +331,8 @@ def eval_func(wrapped, instance, args, kwargs):\n         # retrieve common options from kwargs, and fall back on the command\n         # class attributes, or general defaults if needed\n         common_params = {\n-            p_name: kwargs.pop(\n-                p_name,\n-                getattr(_func_class, p_name, eval_defaults[p_name]))\n+            p_name: kwargs.pop(p_name, None) or \\\n+            getattr(_func_class, p_name, eval_defaults[p_name])\n             for p_name in eval_params}\n         # short cuts and configured setup for common options\n         on_failure = common_params['on_failure']\n```\n\nthen my result filter works was expected.\n\n```\n% datalad -ldebug foo\n[DEBUG  ] Determined class of decorated function: \u003cclass 'datalad.plugin.foo.Foo'\u003e\nfoo(ok): nowhere (dataset) [has blah]\n[DEBUG  ] not reporting result (excluded by filter [utils.py:_process_results:525])\naction summary:\n  foo (ok: 2)\n```\n\nIs there a bug in how the result filter is being processed, or is there something else I need to do to set up the filter?","files":null}]}